## Instruments

Three, as in the rest of the group, but this case's subject IS instrument 1:

1. **The DUT's own log**, read on the console with
   `show log | include tacplus|tacacs|TACACS|TACPLUS`, `show log | include tacplus|FAILED LOGIN|aaa-configure`
   and bounded `show log tail N`.  Filtered on the box and quoted here; never pulled whole
   into the agent's context.  **The IMISH command echoes are removed on the box side after
   the read**, because T33411 measured that a chained `| exclude` is silently swallowed into
   the include pattern on this build.
2. **The server's accounting file** `/var/log/tac_plus.acct`, read in bounded windows with
   `tools/filewin.py`.  This case uses it as the **ground truth for whether an exchange
   actually happened**, so that "the DUT logged nothing" can be separated from "nothing
   happened".  That distinction is the whole of STEP 3.
3. **The wire**, `tools/tb capture ... tcp port 49` decoded with `tools/tcpflow.py --port 49`.

`conlogin.py` (console) and `netlogin.py` (SSH) produce the real logins the authentication
specs need.

## STEP 1 (designed) -- the debug surface: S1599.2.25 and S1599.1.090

Read-only with `qmark.py`, which types `PREFIX ?` with no CR and clears the line.

    awplus# debug ?
      aaa  arp  atmf  bfd  bgp  cfm  dot1x  epsr  fiber-monitoring  g8032  gvrp  hsl  igmp
      ip  ipv6  isis  lacp  ldap  linkmon  lldp  loopprot  mail  mlag  mld  mrp  msdp  mstp
      nsm  ospf  pim  ping-poll  platform  power-inline  private-vlan  ptp  radius  rip
      rmon  sflow  snmp  ssh  stack  trigger  udld  vrrp  wireless

    awplus# debug tacacs ?
    % Unrecognized command

    awplus# debug aaa ?
      accounting      Accounting
      all             Turn on all debugging
      authentication  Authentication
      authorization   Authorization
      <cr>

**STEP 1 VERDICT: PASS, both specifications.**

* **S1599.2.25** -- there is **no `debug tacacs+` command**, and the 47-entry `debug ?` list
  confirms it is a deliberate absence rather than an oversight: `radius`, `ldap` and `dot1x`
  all have their own debug entries, and **TACACS+ is the one AAA protocol without one**.
  That is exactly what the TFS specifies, and it is why every later step in this case matters:
  the log is the only diagnostic this feature has.
* **S1599.1.090** -- `debug aaa` offers precisely `accounting | authentication | authorization
  | all`, the four forms the Feature Page names.

(Tester artefact: the first `qmark` prefix was typed as `--` because no `--mode` was given, so
the console shows `awplus#-- ` answered with `% Unrecognized command` from the help system.
Nothing was executed -- `qmark` sends no CR and clears with Ctrl-U -- and the line was cleared.)

