## NOT MEASURED, and why -- declared, not skipped silently

1. 🔴 **S1599.1.084 and S1599.1.085 -- the log messages for `enable` authentication succeeding
   and failing.**  These are two of the seven specifications this case exists to sweep, and
   they are **NOT MEASURED**, for the reason set out in T33411: producing them requires
   `aaa authentication enable default group tacacs+ ...`, and a rejected `enable` leaves the
   operator at `awplus>` with **no route to configuration mode on any access path** (the
   console and every VTY share one enable method list).  AW+ offers no recovery except a
   reload, and this session forbids a reload because the L3 underlay that carries the path to
   the server exists in running-config only.  The server also has no enable credential for
   these users, so a Reject is the likely outcome.  Raised with the Test Engineer through the
   sentinel at the start of the group so it could be overruled during the run.
   ⇒ **This case covers 5 of the 7 logging specifications.**  The two it does not cover are
   named, not glossed over.
2. **Reboot persistence.**  NOT MEASURED for this group: no reload was performed.
3. **S1599.1.005 / .006 / .007 -- a malformed REPLY being discarded and logged.**  Needs a
   purpose-written server; `tac_plus` is correct by construction and is not ours to modify
   (STANDING-ORDERS §4).
4. **Whether the log buffer retains these messages across a reboot**, and their behaviour
   through a configured remote syslog host.  Neither was exercised.
5. **The permanent log** (`show log permanent`) was not read; only the buffered log.

